fix(spmi): keep the SPMI? report inside the 16 KiB console ring

The first SPMI? run on hardware measured the right values but produced more
output than the USB console can hold: kebab_spmi_report() printed every
non-zero APID mapping entry, the 16 KiB log ring filled, and the capture was
exactly 16383 bytes, cut in the middle of a line.  The command's own summary
and its match list fell off the end; the gate-2 answer was only recoverable
because PON? prints the same three matches first.

The console ring is a hard limit: one command's output is queued in full
before the event thread can drain it, so a report that does not fit is a
report that loses its tail.  SPMI? now prints the scan bounds, the negative
control, the number of entries scanned, the number of non-zero mappings, the
full raw mapping/ownership rows for every APID that maps PPID 0x008, and the
gate result.  That is a few hundred bytes and cannot truncate.  A full table
dump was never needed for the gate and would not fit at any useful size.

The three counts stay in the report so a short capture is self-diagnosing:
scanned entries, non-zero mappings, and matches must all be present, and a
missing tail is visible as a missing gate line rather than silently shorter
output.  No register access changes; SPMI-1/2/3 read exactly the same
registers as 0108.
